Additional notes for the review context — consider these when writing each section:

- The cache uses a defaultdict of Counter, so inserting a key that is absent is implicit. This is convenient but can hide bugs where an unexpected key is queried. A stricter variant would raise or return a typed "miss" object. Assess whether the implicit behavior is a good fit for this use case.
- The save() method serialises int keys as strings (JSON limitation) and the load() method casts them back. Any bug in that round-trip will silently corrupt the cache.[MTP-FINDSLOT] find_slot: n_seq_tokens=512, n_seqs=1, size=1, used=0, head=0
